-- title:
--   Čech cohomology of the quotient twist on a hyperplane section
-- statement:
--   Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and a commutative ring $k$, and write $\mathbb{P}^n_k = \operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded algebra of homogeneous submodules of $k[X_0,\dots,X_n]$, with structure morphism `ProjSpace.π k n` to $\operatorname{Spec} k$.
--
--   The data are: a scheme $Z$ together with a closed immersion $\iota : Z \to \mathbb{P}^n_k$; a polynomial $\ell$ which is homogeneous of degree $1$ (hypothesis `hℓ`); an ideal sheaf datum $\mathcal{I}_\ell$ on $\mathbb{P}^n_k$; a further scheme $Z'$ with a closed immersion $\iota' : Z' \to \mathbb{P}^n_k$; a natural number $d$; and a morphism $\mu$ of the presheaves of modules `ProjSpace.twist` of degrees $d$ and $d+1$ on $Z$.
--
--   Throughout, `ProjSpace.pullbackChart ιk i` is the open $U_i = \iota^{-1}D_+(X_i)$ of $Z$, and for each $i$ the section
--   $$t_i = \iota^\sharp\bigl(\ell/X_i\bigr) \in \Gamma(Z, U_i)$$
--   is the image under `ιk.app` of the section of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{P}^n_k}$ over $D_+(X_i)$ attached by `Proj.awayToSection` to the degree‑$0$ homogeneous localisation with numerator $\ell$ (homogeneous of degree $1$) and denominator $X_i^1$. Similarly `ProjSpace.frameUnit ιk i j` is $u_{ij} = \iota^\sharp(X_j/X_i) \in \Gamma(Z,U_i)$, the image of `ProjSpace.ratio k n i j`. The presheaf `ProjSpace.twist (ιk ≫ ProjSpace.π k n) ιk m` assigns to an open $U \subseteq Z$ the $k$-module of families $(g_i)_{i}$ with $g_i \in \Gamma(Z, U \cap U_i)$ satisfying the frame-compatibility condition `TwistCompat` of degree $m$, with restriction maps acting componentwise; it plays the role of $\mathcal{O}_Z(m)$ described in the standard frames. Finally `ProjSpace.stdCoverPullback ιk` is the ordered affine cover of $Z$ by the opens $U_j$, $j \in \mathrm{Fin}(n+1)$, and for a presheaf $F$ of modules the groups `F.H0 K` and `F.HSucc K i` are the kernel of the $0$-th Čech differential and the quotient $\ker d^{i+1}/\operatorname{im} d^{i}$ for the cover $K$, i.e. $\check H^0$ and $\check H^{i+1}$.
--
--   The hypotheses are as follows.
--
--   (i) Non-zero-divisor hypothesis `hnzd`: for every $i$ and every $t \in \Gamma(Z, U_i)$, $t_i \cdot t = 0$ implies $t = 0$.
--
--   (ii) Hypothesis `h𝓘ℓ` on the ideal sheaf datum: for every $i$, the ideal attached by $\mathcal{I}_\ell$ to the affine open $D_+(X_i)$ equals the ideal generated by the set of all sections of the form `Proj.awayToSection` applied to the degree‑$0$ class $G/X_i^{\,e}$, where $e$ ranges over $\mathbb{N}$ and $G$ over the homogeneous polynomials of degree $e$ lying in the principal ideal $(\ell)$.
--
--   (iii) Hypothesis `hker`: the ideal sheaf datum `ι'.ker` of the closed immersion $\iota'$ is the join $\iota.\mathrm{ker} \sqcup \mathcal{I}_\ell$; thus $Z'$ is the intersection of $Z$ with the hyperplane $\ell = 0$.
--
--   (iv) Cocycle hypothesis `htc`: for all $i, j$, after restriction to $U_i \cap U_j$ one has $t_i = u_{ij}^{1} \cdot t_j$.
--
--   (v) Hypothesis `hμ` describing $\mu$: for every open $U \subseteq Z$, every section $g$ of the degree‑$d$ twist over $U$ and every $i$, the $i$-th component of $\mu_U(g)$ is the restriction of $t_i$ to $U \cap U_i$ times $g_i$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, writing $\mathcal{Q} =$ `OModulePresheaf.coker μ` for the presheaf quotient $U \mapsto \mathcal{O}_Z(d+1)(U)/\operatorname{im}(\mu_U)$, the conclusion asserts the existence of:
--
--   (a) a $k$-linear isomorphism
--   $$e_0 : \check H^0\bigl(\text{stdCoverPullback ιk}, \mathcal{Q}\bigr) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \check H^0\bigl(\text{stdCoverPullback ι'}, \mathcal{O}_{Z'}(d+1)\bigr);$$
--
--   (b) for every $i \in \mathbb{N}$, a $k$-linear isomorphism
--   $$\check H^{i+1}\bigl(\text{stdCoverPullback ιk}, \mathcal{Q}\bigr) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \check H^{i+1}\bigl(\text{stdCoverPullback ι'}, \mathcal{O}_{Z'}(d+1)\bigr),$$
--   this family being bound anonymously, so that no further compatibility is required of it;
--
--   (c) the following normalisation of $e_0$: for every Čech $0$-cochain $c$ of the degree‑$(d+1)$ twist on $Z$ for the cover `stdCoverPullback ιk`, every proof $hc$ that $c$ is a $0$-cocycle, and every polynomial $G$ homogeneous of degree $d+1$, if for every index $s$ of $0$-simplices of the cover and every $i$ the $i$-th component of $c(s)$ is the restriction to $\mathrm{inter}(s) \cap U_i$ of $\iota^\sharp(G/X_i^{\,d+1})$, then for every index $s$ of $0$-simplices of the cover `stdCoverPullback ι'` of $Z'$ and every $i$, the $i$-th component at $s$ of the cochain underlying
--   $$e_0\Bigl( \bigl(\text{(OModulePresheaf.imCokerSES μ).proj}\bigr)^{\!*} \langle c, hc\rangle \Bigr)$$
--   — that is, of the image of the class of $\langle c, hc \rangle$ under the map on $\check H^0$ induced by the quotient projection $\mathcal{O}_Z(d+1) \to \mathcal{Q}$ of the short exact sequence `imCokerSES μ` — is the restriction to $\mathrm{inter}(s) \cap \iota'^{-1}D_+(X_i)$ of $\iota'^\sharp(G/X_i^{\,d+1})$.
--
--   Thus the quotient of the degree‑$(d+1)$ twist on $Z$ by multiplication by $\ell$ from the degree‑$d$ twist has the same Čech groups, for the standard charts, as the degree‑$(d+1)$ twist on the hyperplane section $Z'$, and in degree $0$ the isomorphism matches the cocycles cut out by a single form $G$ of degree $d+1$ on $Z$ and on $Z'$.
--
--   This is the identification of the presheaf cokernel $\mathcal{O}_Z(d+1)/\ell\,\mathcal{O}_Z(d)$ with $\mathcal{O}_{Z'}(d+1)$, $Z' = Z \cap V(\ell)$, at the level of Čech cohomology for the charts pulled back from the standard cover of $\mathbb{P}^n_k$, together with the compatibility of the degree‑$0$ isomorphism with the classes of forms of degree $d+1$. It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.exists_affSES_twist_succ_of_forall_mul_eq_zero_imp`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.exists_affSES_twist_succ_of_forall_mul_eq_zero_imp), in the construction of the short exact sequence of twists by a linear form that underlies the cohomological regularity estimates for projective schemes in the project.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_ProjSpace_exists_linearEquiv_H0_HSucc_coker_twist_of_ker_eq_sup.lean

